course: dictionary
lesson: 9348
title: Splash: a word that sounds like its meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Splash can be an action word (a verb) or a thing you can count (a noun). Read the words around it to find which one fits. «They watch him splash past, rolling badly but rowing his hardest.» Here splash is an action: he is moving through water and sending drops flying.
explain: Splash also sounds like what it means. Words like this are called onomatopoeia. «Her foot slips and "splash! she was up to her chin in salt water".» Say splash out loud and you can hear the water hitting something.
explain: Splash can also mean more than water. «A splash of colour» is a small bright patch, and «to make a splash» means to get a lot of attention. Ask yourself: is there water, colour, or people noticing? The clues tell you which meaning to use.
fact: «Splash» can be a verb (to splash) or a noun (a splash).
fact: «To splash» means to hit water or another liquid so that drops fly about.
fact: «A splash» is the sound or movement of liquid hitting something, or a small spot of liquid.
fact: «A splash of colour» is a small bright patch of colour.
fact: «To make a splash» means to get a lot of attention.
exercise: «They watch him splash past, rolling badly but rowing his hardest.» What does splash mean here? | To shout loudly at a friend | To sleep quietly on a soft bed | To paint a wall white | *To move through water, sending drops flying
exercise: «Her foot slips and "splash!" she was up to her chin in salt water.» Splash sounds like the noise it names. What is that kind of word called? | *Onomatopoeia | Synonym | Homophone | Antonym
exercise: Ella says «a splash of colour» means the paint has spilled all over the floor. What does it really mean? | *A small bright patch of colour | A loud noise in the kitchen | A sudden storm of rain | A large dark stain on the floor
test: «If paint splashes in your eye, rinse it with clean water and tell an adult.» What does splashes mean here? | To close your eyes tightly | To sing a song loudly | *Liquid flies out and lands on something | To rub gently with a cloth
test: Jayden says, «He made a splash at school with his science project.» What does made a splash mean? | He jumped into the school pool | He spilled a drink on the floor | He washed the science table | *He got a lot of attention
exam: Why is splash an onomatopoeia? | Because it means the opposite of dry | Because it is the name of a place | Because it comes from another language | *Because the word sounds like the noise of liquid hitting something
